{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"resume-assistant","displayName":"Resume Assistant","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/wscats/skills/resume-assistant","publisherHandle":"wscats","publisherDisplayName":"enoyao","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/wscats","version":"1.0.6","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1773461889571,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/resume-assistant/card?ownerHandle=wscats&version=1.0.6","sha256":"29f1f03f41aef32244b73f92ad16f35d09ac811ff0e05c49df6a73934e06cb4a","size":2468,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"8d29c8efe7d5408b59e95e09b8e163fb0ff41a10561c6abc5e4fde08048f944f","bundleFingerprints":["cbc26f66edfc2fa28956e0183485ffe73cf5a82cd24103eab38ac8c31994f8bf","66765aa09c14b6bb806674d116611e81eae3ada83ff392fad2b3be6c70418672"],"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":10640,"sha256":"2a7d4a44855014301619d992ac84f4f1637bb7959130e68c598fd54f805ba4c3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README_ZH.md","size":10688,"sha256":"8eddc50fccf430b016c8bed8dec686a6f951b34f3fe831603beb05e126dcf242","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":18826,"sha256":"224bae2d8dfd1c11c0d28cba8337bc7754a19278b1c9c4119fdded501b1559e5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL_ZH.md","size":22825,"sha256":"c9befe88ba51e0a46f97ddf8c5913b37821e362d4f9bf02ae91e9b68f30d9e7a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/sample-resume-en.md","size":2525,"sha256":"eca2b913a2060778695cf6ff98d9290039279ed66c360661852bf4af4d62ef36","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/sample-resume-weak.md","size":781,"sha256":"169e05ee728f28ba2aca16882e21093aecf0bed1cf5ed29c2ddee60425e6e0f1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/sample-resume-zh.md","size":2290,"sha256":"a485009f0ee071461e741a3039bfe5c6c0b1ece9f8a83356e0b36a72a8f7ad55","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/usage.md","size":7748,"sha256":"76b48aaabb1bb5ef16a3b6e2ca5ce8e10406076405c7aea1ef0effe358a184a1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/customize.md","size":3557,"sha256":"2aa3d51c5685c3d12284a471d4b0a0947d2dd3156997e969f0923adc95332876","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/export.md","size":4124,"sha256":"1744286c7c7a15d6d5994051fb282e03e14469dc89d82bdbc394d6d318e5d50e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/polish.md","size":5259,"sha256":"0ec34ba4f6b7fa6f327e54eaff1456185563a7667850ea632d8c0f31171534fb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/score.md","size":5605,"sha256":"17a6bfedf28a07da324fcd2b8789e064f98d23eefcc34d059f821d120c935f38","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/system.md","size":5192,"sha256":"a3abebb727769c52b9710627fcd738ce5b44321e41caa3a341df43514358a658","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill.json","size":5659,"sha256":"5064b315222c2b070ff04af233413787f5ed93dfe05116a469675e301ea04c91","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill.yaml","size":5862,"sha256":"1c50241f7e89f949fce91774d56d6d0cb9d0ee3eb4046e199779f6469446feed","contentType":"text/yaml"},{"path":"templates/academic.md","size":1491,"sha256":"e2cccf18ee9ba0160c9eb57a837ed8c4d30a989854d9d27a1f3e6477aa849f44","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"templates/export/resume.html","size":5886,"sha256":"7b4835eb57b4a30cbe66b1f9180d2e54f88315916430ffcabe707be7435d015c","contentType":"text/html"},{"path":"templates/minimal.md","size":625,"sha256":"1ca9877b55ba7d8302e4b3997c58d3789ca93dbea120e6b353322caf04d37649","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"templates/modern.md","size":1131,"sha256":"3ec6b35519ab859e1480859a3d3349119c0168a52de529a8ebd32f5698245265","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"templates/professional.md","size":850,"sha256":"0ddee20da4ac4932efa15186006b4f222e9d7e29a3cd4e3230d7000e2d535919","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent resume-assistant prompt package, with no hidden execution or persistence, but users should handle resume data and HTML exports carefully.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789175407041,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unescaped User-Controlled Data in Exported HTML Resume"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"templates/export/resume.html"},"region":{"startLine":113,"endLine":166}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"9b11e2598278a86f"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `templates/export/resume.html:113-166`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: HTML injection and potential cross-site scripting in generated documents  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```html\n<div class=\"resume {{template_class}}\">\n\n    <div class=\"header\">\n        <h1>{{name}}</h1>\n        <div class=\"contact\">\n            {{email}} <span class=\"sep\">·</span> {{phone}} <span class=\"sep\">·</span> {{location}}\n            <br>\n            <a href=\"{{linkedin}}\">LinkedIn</a> <span class=\"sep\">·</span> <a href=\"{{portfolio}}\">Portfolio</a>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"section\">\n        <h2>Professional Summary</h2>\n        <p>{{summary}}</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"section\">\n        <h2>Experience</h2>\n        <!-- Repeat .entry for each position -->\n        <div class=\"entry\">\n            <div class=\"row\">\n                <span class=\"title\">{{job_title}}</span>\n                <span class=\"meta\">{{start_date}} – {{end_date}}</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"row\">\n                <span class=\"company\">{{company}}</span>\n                <span class=\"meta\">{{location}}</span>\n            </div>\n            <ul>\n                <li>{{bullet}}</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"section\">\n        <h2>Education</h2>\n        <div class=\"entry\">\n            <div class=\"row\">\n                <span class=\"title\">{{degree}} in {{major}}</span>\n                <span class=\"meta\">{{graduation_date}}</span>\n            </div>\n            <span class=\"company\">{{university}}</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"section\">\n        <h2>Skills</h2>\n        <div class=\"skills-grid\">\n            <span class=\"cat\">Technical:</span>\n            <span class=\"val\">{{technical_skills}}</span>\n            <span class=\"cat\">Tools:</span>\n            <span class=\"val\">{{tools}}</span>\n            <span class=\"cat\">Languages:</span>\n            <span class=\"val\">{{languages}}</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe HTML export template places resume-derived values directly into several security-sensitive contexts:\n\n- HTML text nodes, including `{{name}}`, `{{summary}}`, `{{bullet}}`, and skill fields.\n- HTML attributes, including `{{template_class}}`.\n- URL attributes, including `{{linkedin}}` and `{{portfolio}}`.\n\nThe project does not document or enforce contextual output encoding for these placeholders. If the integration populates this template through direct string replacement, a maliciously crafted resume value can terminate its intended HTML context and inject arbitrary markup or event-handler attributes.\n\nFor example, a text field containing the following value could introduce active HTML if inserted without escaping:\n\n```html\n</p><img src=x onerror=\"alert(document.domain)\"><p>\n```\n\nA link field can also use an unsafe scheme:\n\n```text\njavascript:alert(document.domain)\n```\n\nThis is particularly relevant because the generated HTML is intended to be opened in a browser and may also be shared with recruiters or other third parties. The repository does not include a rendering implementation, so exploitation depends on the consuming agent or application performing unescaped substitution. Nevertheless, the template itself provides no safe rendering contract or validation requirement.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker supplies a resume, profile URL, summary, employment bullet, or other field containing crafted HTML or a dangerous URL scheme.\n2. A compatible agent invokes the HTML or PDF export workflow.\n3. The consuming application populates `templates/export/resume.html` using direct or otherwise non-escaping placeholder substitution.\n4. The resulting HTML contains attacker-controlled elements, attributes, or links.\n5. The generated resume is opened by the user or sent to a recruiter.\n6. An injected event handler may execute when the document is rendered, or a `javascript:` link may execute when clicked.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation can execute attacker-controlled JavaScript within the security context assigned to the generated document by the browser. Depending on how the file is served or opened, possible effects include:\n\n- Modification of the displayed resume content.\n- Phishing or deceptive user-interface injection.\n- Malicious redirects or execution through unsafe links.\n- Access to same-origin application data if the generated document is served from an authenticated application origin.\n- Access to browser-permitted local resources or document contents when opened as a local file.\n- Propagation of a malicious exported resume to recruiters or other recipients.\n\nThis issue does not directly grant operating-system privileges. Its scope is primarily the generated document and the browser origin or local-file permissions under which that document is opened.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Use a maintained template engine with automatic HTML escaping enabled by default. Do not populate the template with direct string replacement.\n2. Apply context-specific encoding:\n   - HTML-escape all values inserted into text nodes.\n   - Attribute-escape values inserted into HTML attributes.\n   - Validate and normalize all URL values before placing them in `href`.\n3. Allowlist URL schemes such as `https:`, `http:`, and, where necessary, `mailto:`. Explicitly reject `javascript:`, `data:`, `vbscript:`, and malformed or control-character-obfuscated schemes.\n4. Restrict `template_class` to the documented values:\n   - `professional`\n   - `modern`\n   - `minimal`\n   - `academic`\n5. If limited rich text is intentionally supported, sanitize it with a proven HTML sanitizer using a restrictive element and attribute allowlist. Do not permit event-handler attributes, scripts, iframes, embedded objects, or arbitrary CSS.\n6. Add a Content Security Policy when serving generated resumes from a web application. A restrictive baseline should disallow scripts and embedded objects, for example:\n\n```http\nContent-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data: https:; font-src data:; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'\n```\n\n7. Prefer serving generated resumes from a sandboxed, cookieless origin rather than the authenticated application origin.\n8. Add automated tests covering text-node, attribute, and URL payloads, including:\n\n```text\n\"><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>\n</p><script>alert(1)</script><p>\njavascript:alert(1)\njava&#x73;cript:alert(1)\n```\n\nThe tests should verify that injected markup is rendered as inert text and that unsafe links are rejected.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789175254.8358548,"endTime":1789175357.0974085}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"unknown","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57ftnw4ez25gxnm030f52ekgd8e90bp-dPljSh/clawscan-skillspector-1829439629/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-12T01:07:33.303467+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":86,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":297,"executable":false,"size_bytes":10640,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"README_ZH.md","type":"markdown","lines":307,"executable":false,"size_bytes":10688,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":532,"executable":false,"size_bytes":18826,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL_ZH.md","type":"markdown","lines":628,"executable":false,"size_bytes":22825,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/sample-resume-en.md","type":"markdown","lines":65,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2525,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/sample-resume-weak.md","type":"markdown","lines":36,"executable":false,"size_bytes":781,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/sample-resume-zh.md","type":"markdown","lines":65,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2290,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/usage.md","type":"markdown","lines":228,"executable":false,"size_bytes":7748,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"prompts/customize.md","type":"markdown","lines":135,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3557,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"prompts/export.md","type":"markdown","lines":137,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4124,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"prompts/polish.md","type":"markdown","lines":184,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5259,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"prompts/score.md","type":"markdown","lines":189,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5605,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"prompts/system.md","type":"markdown","lines":98,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5192,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"skill.json","type":"json","lines":194,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5659,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"skill.yaml","type":"yaml","lines":206,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5862,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"templates/academic.md","type":"markdown","lines":83,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1491,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"templates/export/resume.html","type":"other","lines":172,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5886,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"templates/minimal.md","type":"markdown","lines":37,"executable":false,"size_bytes":625,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"templates/modern.md","type":"markdown","lines":61,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1131,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"templates/professional.md","type":"markdown","lines":53,"executable":false,"size_bytes":850,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"P2","finding_id":"finding-bce21b54d46d4cfa85fc14463c35c332","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Hidden Instructions","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"templates/academic.md","start_line":78,"end_line":null},"finding":"<!-- Template: Academic\n     Style: Formal academic CV, multi-page supported\n     Best for: Faculty, postdoc, research, PhD applications\n     Font suggestion: Times New Roman 11pt or Garamond 11pt\n   ","explanation":"Hidden instructions were detected in comments or invisible text. These could contain malicious directives. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Audit all comments and invisible characters. Remove any instructions that direct the agent to perform unauthorized actions. Use plain, reviewable content.","code_snippet":"\n---\n\n<!-- Template: Academic\n     Style: Formal academic CV, multi-page supported\n     Best for: Faculty, postdoc, research, PhD applications\n     Font suggestion: Times New Roman 11pt or Garamond 11pt","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"99ddac2bc96870a1c21b359f46353712eb8adfb276bd9990d469c6b8a1f08f98","occurrences":[{"file":"templates/academic.md","start_line":78,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P2","finding_id":"finding-d3322648c0674c99af74fc90507f690a","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Hidden Instructions","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"templates/minimal.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null},"finding":"<!-- Template: Minimal\n     Style: Ultra-clean, whitespace-focused, maximum content density\n     Best for: Senior professionals, engineering, experienced candidates\n     Font suggestion: System UI 11p","explanation":"Hidden instructions were detected in comments or invisible text. These could contain malicious directives. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Audit all comments and invisible characters. Remove any instructions that direct the agent to perform unauthorized actions. Use plain, reviewable content.","code_snippet":"\n---\n\n<!-- Template: Minimal\n     Style: Ultra-clean, whitespace-focused, maximum content density\n     Best for: Senior professionals, engineering, experienced candidates\n     Font suggestion: System UI 11pt","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"72138f2254eb43a143cfb90d6bd41542e434310b3e5a4700e40dc04b3740212c","occurrences":[{"file":"templates/minimal.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-64f9e1249c8545acad3539d2e565d504","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":33,"end_line":46},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README encourages very broad natural-language triggering using common phrases like 'Here's my resume, can you help?' and 'What's wrong with my resume?'. In agent environments that auto-route skills based on user text, this can cause unintended invocation and accidental processing of sensitive resume data without clear user confirmation.","remediation":"Narrow the invocation guidance to explicit commands or clearly scoped trigger phrases, and require confirmation before processing uploaded resume content. Document how intent detection is bounded, and prefer opt-in activation such as '/resume ...' over ambiguous everyday language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":33,"end_line":46}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-32946896a616434da7dbbe4d0b5f5137","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":174,"end_line":183},"finding":null,"explanation":"The integration section shows resume content being sent to an API endpoint, but the README does not warn users that highly sensitive personal data may be transmitted to external services. Because resumes commonly contain contact details, employment history, and other PII, users may unknowingly expose private information to third-party processing.","remediation":"Add a prominent privacy notice stating that resume content may be transmitted to external APIs or hosted LLM services for processing. Document what data is sent, where it goes, retention/logging expectations, and provide guidance for redacting sensitive fields or using local/self-hosted deployments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":174,"end_line":183}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-78946c63e35d48248fc399f3478c91aa","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":177,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST https://your-agent-api.com/skills/resume-assistant/polish \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"### Option 3: REST API\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://your-agent-api.com/skills/resume-assistant/polish \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"resume_content\": \"Your resume content...\",","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"bac1047453aeda63b217125b880ef48c312a9644b8b86a3520644cded196969b","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":177,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-78946c63e35d48248fc399f3478c91aa","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"README_ZH.md","start_line":187,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST https://your-agent-api.com/skills/resume-assistant/polish \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"### Option 3: REST API\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://your-agent-api.com/skills/resume-assistant/polish \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"resume_content\": \"Your resume content...\",","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"bac1047453aeda63b217125b880ef48c312a9644b8b86a3520644cded196969b","occurrences":[{"file":"README_ZH.md","start_line":187,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-ce529c8f66e24e10a5543ec89cf82bb2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"README_ZH.md","start_line":35,"end_line":56},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README encourages very broad natural-language triggering such as '帮我看看' or '这是我的简历，帮我看看', which can cause the agent to invoke this skill from ordinary conversation without strong user confirmation or parameter validation. In an agent environment with automatic routing, this increases the chance of unintended processing of sensitive resume data or accidental execution of export/customization flows.","remediation":"Narrow the invocation examples to clearly resume-specific intents, require explicit confirmation before acting on ambiguous phrases, and document recommended routing safeguards. Add examples showing that export, transmission, or file-writing actions require explicit user consent and structured parameters.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README_ZH.md","start_line":35,"end_line":56}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-3a74623d141549998431fb26fe346d51","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":35},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill advertises activation through very broad natural-language phrases such as general resume-help requests, which overlap heavily with ordinary conversation. In an agent environment that auto-routes tools from user intent, this can cause unintended invocation on sensitive resume content or job descriptions without an explicit opt-in boundary.","remediation":"Narrow activation phrases and require explicit tool invocation cues such as '/resume ...' or a confirmed resume-specific intent. Add disambiguation logic before running the skill, e.g. confirm the user wants the resume tool when the request is generic like 'can you help?' or 'what do you think?'.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":22,"end_line":35}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-ef6ebf1652884bd29298994b3183f8bb","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":202,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST https://your-agent-api.com/skills/resume-assistant/polish \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"resume_content\": \"Your resume content...\",\n    \"language\": \"en\"\n  }'\n\n# Sc","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n```bash\n# Polish a resume\ncurl -X POST https://your-agent-api.com/skills/resume-assistant/polish \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"resume_content\": \"Your resume content...\",","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"dc4ac9fc7972e0cc2b111f6718438de99459d13f4174f5fd76cad85d06598971","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":202,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-d5d0dbf206064cc9a0c809090d515640","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":283,"end_line":297},"finding":null,"explanation":"The routing keywords are generic terms like 'fix', 'job', 'download', and 'evaluate', which are common across many agent tasks. In a multi-skill agent, this increases the chance that unrelated user requests are misrouted into this skill, potentially exposing private content or causing inappropriate transformations/exports.","remediation":"Use more specific intent classifiers tied to resume-related entities and require both domain and action matches before invocation. Add precedence rules and a confirmation step when keywords are ambiguous, especially for broad terms like 'help', 'fix', 'export', or 'score'.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":283,"end_line":297}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-deeb5b5165e74974a139b84f5477048d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL_ZH.md","start_line":23,"end_line":33},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill advertises very broad natural-language triggers such as '这是我的简历，帮我看看' and '帮我写一份…', with no explicit scoping or confirmation step. In an agent that auto-routes skills based on conversational text, this can cause accidental invocation on ordinary chat content or pasted documents, potentially leading to unintended processing of sensitive resume data or unwanted actions like export/customization flows.","remediation":"Narrow trigger phrases and require explicit user intent confirmation before invoking the skill, especially for document-processing actions. Add negative examples, routing constraints, and a mandatory confirmation step when a resume-like blob is detected or when the agent is inferring intent from ambiguous language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_ZH.md","start_line":23,"end_line":33}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-af72a45518f5461dab6d2c65bf4e4a50","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL_ZH.md","start_line":211,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST https://your-agent-api.com/skills/resume-assistant/polish \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"resume_content\": \"你的简历内容...\",\n    \"language\": \"zh\"\n  }'\n\n# 简历评分\ncurl -X PO","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n```bash\n# 简历润色\ncurl -X POST https://your-agent-api.com/skills/resume-assistant/polish \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"resume_content\": \"你的简历内容...\",","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f37f360b958344f11d8b68c6fa98e2849ebd9c52a5f7a5c93d8188b126467c57","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_ZH.md","start_line":211,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-ba6e85ca293b4e08a6de7cd8f46593d2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL_ZH.md","start_line":292,"end_line":306},"finding":null,"explanation":"The routing logic maps generic concepts like '润色/优化/修改', '求职/申请/匹配', and '导出/下载/转换' directly to commands without disambiguation rules. In a multi-skill agent, these broad intent buckets can overmatch unrelated user requests and trigger processing or transformation of user content that was not meant for this skill.","remediation":"Define strict routing boundaries with required entities, negative examples, and precedence rules across skills. Prefer explicit command invocation or ask a clarifying question before routing when the request contains generic verbs or overlaps with other skills.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_ZH.md","start_line":292,"end_line":306}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-00900da2e3784e97899eeeaac033e8dc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"examples/usage.md","start_line":4,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill advertises very broad natural-language triggers such as 'Here's my resume, can you help?' and 'What's wrong with my resume?', which can cause accidental or overbroad invocation in normal conversation. This increases the chance users will paste sensitive resume or job-description data without clearly understanding they are invoking a workflow that may process and transform personal information.","remediation":"Narrow invocation phrases and clearly separate example utterances from actual activation patterns. Add explicit user-facing guidance that resume/job-description content may contain sensitive personal data, and require clearer intent confirmation before processing large pasted documents.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/usage.md","start_line":4,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8600c091b2cf40b092458cb3d91169cb","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"examples/usage.md","start_line":4,"end_line":228},"finding":null,"explanation":"The usage guidance encourages users to submit resumes, job descriptions, employment history, education, and other potentially sensitive personal data, but it does not warn users about privacy considerations or recommend redacting unnecessary identifiers. In a resume-assistant context this omission is meaningful because the core workflow is built around collecting and processing high-value personal and professional information.","remediation":"Add a prominent privacy notice explaining that resumes and job descriptions may contain sensitive personal data and advising users to avoid sharing unnecessary identifiers such as full address, phone number, personal email, government IDs, or confidential employer information. Provide redaction guidance, data-minimization recommendations, and a short consent/awareness prompt before users paste documents.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/usage.md","start_line":4,"end_line":228}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-46e011f2d5c642359c73c693d6c85043","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"skill.json","start_line":21,"end_line":25},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest sets the optional \"language\" argument default to \"en\" for multiple commands, which means the skill will prefer English unless the user overrides it. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without explicit user choice can be a natural-language policy violation when no justification or opt-in is provided.","remediation":"Remove the hardcoded English default, infer language from the user's input when possible, or require explicit user selection before choosing a language. Alternatively, document a justified locale constraint if the skill is intentionally English-first.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skill.json","start_line":21,"end_line":25}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-8ad9b197f93245a181109d2267319977","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skill.json","start_line":140,"end_line":192},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language triggers are broad phrases such as 'convert to', 'save as', 'create a resume for', and 'review my resume', which can match ordinary conversation and cause the skill to activate when the user did not explicitly intend to invoke it. In a resume assistant, unintended activation can lead to incorrect routing of user input, accidental processing of sensitive resume/job-description content, and confusion or policy bypass in multi-skill environments.","remediation":"Narrow trigger phrases to more explicit, high-intent invocations, require stronger contextual matching (for example, presence of 'resume' plus an action), and prefer explicit command invocation for destructive or high-scope actions like export/customize. Add disambiguation prompts before activation when a trigger is ambiguous, and test trigger collisions against common non-skill conversation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skill.json","start_line":140,"end_line":192}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-293fd49ee867472dbdb007450ccbc1d5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"skill.yaml","start_line":30,"end_line":34},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest repeatedly states that resume language is only 'en' or 'zh' and defaults to English, while supported_languages is restricted to those two values. This is a language/locale policy concern because the skill appears to force a limited language set without user opt-in or a documented region-specific justification.","remediation":"Allow open-ended language selection where feasible, or clearly document why the skill is intentionally limited to English and Chinese and require explicit user choice rather than defaulting silently to English.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skill.yaml","start_line":30,"end_line":34}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-36b26eb8edf144f5b804de54a7707da1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"skill.yaml","start_line":158,"end_line":206},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language triggers include generic phrases such as \"convert to\", \"save as\", \"create a resume for\", and \"review my resume\" that can match ordinary user utterances without clearly scoped command intent. This can cause unintended command routing or over-activation, especially where export/customize actions may process sensitive resume content or job descriptions unexpectedly.","remediation":"Narrow trigger phrases to explicit, high-intent patterns such as \"export my resume to PDF\" or \"customize my resume for this job\". Add disambiguation logic requiring resume-specific context plus explicit action/format, and prefer confirmation before executing export or customization when a trigger is ambiguous.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skill.yaml","start_line":158,"end_line":206}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0ded44831dd24633a969e634c375a0bd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"README_ZH.md","start_line":24,"end_line":27},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation advertises export to Word, HTML, LaTeX, and PDF without warning that user-supplied resume content will be transformed into generated artifacts, potentially written to disk or passed through conversion tooling. While the README alone does not perform the export, omitting safety expectations can lead integrators to enable output generation on sensitive personal data without adequate consent, sanitization, or secure handling.","remediation":"Add explicit warnings that export operations transform and may write personal data to files or external converters. Document safe handling requirements: obtain user consent, sanitize content for template/rendering contexts, restrict output paths, and avoid invoking unsafe converters on untrusted input.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README_ZH.md","start_line":24,"end_line":27}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-7b83fec54bd443f2b1a2f6b010d5f56b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"SKILL_ZH.md","start_line":588,"end_line":609},"finding":null,"explanation":"文档明确仅“完整支持” `en` 和 `zh`，配置中 `supported_languages` 也只列出这两种语言，但未说明是否允许用户保留其他语言输入、获得降级支持，或该限制为何必要。对通用简历技能而言，这种语言范围限制若无明确用户选择或正当范围说明，可能构成语言/locale 政策问题。","remediation":"明确说明语言支持是能力边界而非强制策略，并提供用户可选项与降级行为，例如保留原语言、提示当前仅优化中英文、或请求用户确认是否切换到受支持语言。","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_ZH.md","start_line":588,"end_line":609}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1daf47d86da748c2a7b773efce7ac2f8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"examples/sample-resume-zh.md","start_line":1,"end_line":65},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file is entirely presented in Chinese and functions as a language-specific skill/example without indicating that the user can choose another language or that the scope is intentionally China/Chinese-locale only. Under the policy rule for natural-language violations, a fixed language can be an issue when no opt-in or justification is provided.","remediation":"Document that this file is a Chinese-language example intended for zh users, or explicitly offer alternative language versions or user language selection in surrounding skill documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/sample-resume-zh.md","start_line":1,"end_line":65}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-90d42ce929e54ff4a2ea159ccb1dce88","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"prompts/polish.md","start_line":75,"end_line":75},"finding":null,"explanation":"The checklist includes a locale-specific requirement, 'For zh: proper spacing between Chinese and English/numbers,' which introduces a language-specific policy expectation inside a general resume-polishing prompt. Although the file accepts a {{language}} input, it does not explicitly frame this as an optional user choice or justify the locale constraint, so it can be read as enforcing a specific language convention.","remediation":"Clarify that language and locale rules are applied only when the user explicitly selects that language/locale, e.g. 'If the user-selected language is zh, apply Chinese typography spacing conventions.'","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"prompts/polish.md","start_line":75,"end_line":75}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-510e5fcd332142088d8d700620e0f791","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"prompts/score.md","start_line":11,"end_line":11},"finding":null,"explanation":"The prompt includes a required output/input language field (`{{language}}`), which can enforce a specific language or locale in the skill behavior. The file does not state that the user selected this language or that language choice is optional, so it presents a mild natural-language policy concern under locale-choice rules.","remediation":"Clarify that the language is user-selected or optional, such as: 'Respond in the user's chosen language if provided; otherwise default to the conversation language.'","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"prompts/score.md","start_line":11,"end_line":11}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-f3c8168ea66542308fcae98f4fd0e7d9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"skill.json","start_line":123,"end_line":139},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest advertises only \"en\" and \"zh\" in supported languages and provides conversation starters only in those languages. While not inherently unsafe, this can amount to a language/locale policy issue because the skill appears to constrain language support without an explicit opt-in or clear justification.","remediation":"State clearly that the skill currently supports English and Chinese only, and present language selection as an explicit user choice. If broader language support is not available, document the limitation and rationale in the user-facing description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skill.json","start_line":123,"end_line":139}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-baa026904df54269b1e45ace60e55112","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"skill.yaml","start_line":143,"end_line":153},"finding":null,"explanation":"Examples like \"Create a resume for a software engineer position\" and \"Polish my resume and fix any issues\" are natural everyday requests and do not clarify when they should map to specific commands versus general assistance. In a manifest file, this can contribute to ambiguous activation behavior when combined with permissive natural-language triggers.","remediation":"Make example invocations more explicit about the intended command or context, such as pairing each starter with a specific slash command or adding wording that limits interpretation to this skill's supported actions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skill.yaml","start_line":143,"end_line":153}]},{"id":"EA3","finding_id":"finding-78f001c2451e44fd92c9f1e4efa04fe9","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Scope Creep","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"templates/academic.md","start_line":83,"end_line":null},"finding":"NOT limited to","explanation":"Skill's behavior or capabilities extend beyond its stated purpose. Scope creep allows an agent to perform actions unrelated to its documented functionality, increasing the attack surface.","remediation":"Limit the skill's scope to its documented purpose. Remove instructions that enable the agent to perform actions outside its stated functionality.","code_snippet":"     Best for: Faculty, p